{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T05:27:31Z","timestamp":1772256451290,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2001,11,22]],"date-time":"2001-11-22T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1006387200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc-sa\/2.5\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Atmos. Chem. Phys."],"abstract":"<jats:p>Abstract. The kinetics of the title reactions were investigated using the laser photolysis - resonance fluorescence method, employing the sequential two-photon dissociation of NO2 in the presence of H2\u00a0 as the OH source. The 298 K rate constant for OH + C3H8 was found to be (1.15 \u00b1 0.1) \u00d7 10-12 cm3 s-1, in excellent agreement with the literature recommendation, and with a separate determination using HNO3\u00a0 photolysis at 248 nm as the OH source. The 298 K rate constants for OH + n - C3H7I and\u00a0 i - C3H7I\u00a0 were measured for the first time and found to be (1.47 \u00b1 0.08) and (1.22 \u00b1 0.06) \u00d7 10-12 cm3 s-1, respectively. The errors include an assessment of systematic error due to concentration measurement, which, for the propyl-iodides was minimised by on-line UV-absorption spectroscopy. These results show that reaction with OH is an important sink for\u00a0 n - C3H7I and\u00a0 i - C3H7I, which has implications for the reactive iodine budget of the marine boundary layer.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5194\/acp-1-1-2001","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,4,29]],"date-time":"2010-04-29T09:33:10Z","timestamp":1272533590000},"page":"1-7","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["298 K rate coefficients for the reaction of OH with\n                    <i>i<\/i>\n                    - C\n                    <sub>3<\/sub>\n                    H\n                    <sub>7<\/sub>\n                    I,\n                    <i>n<\/i>\n                    - C\n                    <sub>3<\/sub>\n                    H\n                    <sub>7<\/sub>\n                    I and C\n                    <sub>3<\/sub>\n                    H\n                    <sub>8<\/sub>"],"prefix":"10.5194","volume":"1","author":[{"given":"S. A.","family":"Carl","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"J. N.","family":"Crowley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3145","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2001,11,22]]},"container-title":["Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/acp.copernicus.org\/articles\/1\/1\/2001\/acp-1-1-2001.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,2,16]],"date-time":"2025-02-16T05:38:02Z","timestamp":1739684282000},"score":1,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/acp.copernicus.org\/articles\/1\/1\/2001\/"}},"subtitle":[],"short-title":[],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2001,11,22]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2001]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5194\/acp-1-1-2001","relation":{"has-preprint":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.5194\/acpd-1-23-2001","asserted-by":"subject"},{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.5194\/acpd-1-23-2001","asserted-by":"object"}]},"ISSN":["1680-7324"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1680-7324","type":"electronic"}],"subject":[],"published":{"date-parts":[[2001,11,22]]}}}